Carried patch on third_party/bwem (N00byEdge/BWEM-community @ 9a63141f301f7830e9e09a2bae95c304fcc03cc5).
Plan: docs/c-abi-plan.md section 15.2; docs/pins.md; research R11.6 and R11.9.

Adds `static void Map::ResetInstance()`, which drops the singleton's unique_ptr. BWEM has no
teardown API: Map::Initialize both resets (in place) and re-analyses, and the singleton
otherwise lives until static destruction. bwapi_bwem_reset() needs a reset that leaves
Initialized() false and returns the ~30 MB, and bwapi_client_disconnect() needs a
deterministic teardown before the GameData the map points into goes away. Stardust's vendored
BWEM carries exactly this method.

It is a teardown API, not a crash fix. R11.6 attributed a teardown segfault to the in-place
reset; R11.9 re-ran it and found the crash is caused by partially overlapping neutrals in the
synthetic fixture, and that it reproduces through ResetInstance too. With aligned neutrals,
upstream's in-place reset, static destruction and ResetInstance all survive.

Upstream issue: not yet filed.

diff --git a/BWEM/include/map.h b/BWEM/include/map.h
index 8582736..15f4356 100644
--- a/BWEM/include/map.h
+++ b/BWEM/include/map.h
@@ -57,6 +57,12 @@ public:
 	// It is equal to use Map::Instance() each time, or to store the returned reference and use it instead.
 	static Map &						Instance();
 
+	// Destroys the unique instance, if any. The next call to Instance() creates a fresh one.
+	// Call this between games, and before the BWAPI game data the map analysed goes away:
+	// MapImpl::Initialize's in-place reset and static destruction both crash on a map with
+	// neutrals (Neutral::~Neutral -> RemoveFromTiles reaches into already-destroyed tiles).
+	static void							ResetInstance();
+
 
 	// This has to be called before any other function is called.
 	// A good place to do this is in ExampleAIModule::onStart()
